      "content": "thanks. i'll try letting it sit for a day. one more thing though—i've noticed that even when i'm being super careful with the angle, it feels like the wood almost 'resists' certain spots, like it's fighting the chisel. is it normal for the grain to behave that inconsistently in a single piece of high-end walnut, or is that a sign of something more fundamental going on with the timber?",
